@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
allowmixing
hide circle
hide empty methods
top to bottom direction
title Tutorial 1 · Locate the card and both functions in one package
folder "tutorial::lifetime\nversion 1" as lifetime_pkg #E8F3EB {
  class "Card\nresource declaration" as card {
    Opaque handle; internal layout is private
  }
  class "create_card\nfunction declaration" as create_card {
    No parameters
    result : nullable<Card> (Card or null)
  }
  class "destroy_card\nfunction declaration" as destroy_card {
    card : Card (parameter)
    result : unit (no result value)
  }
  card -down-> destroy_card : lifecycle(unique, @destroy_card)
  card -[hidden]right-> create_card
}
legend bottom
  Folder = named, versioned package; compartmented box = declaration.
  All three declarations belong directly to the package.
  Read each function's parameters and result within its own box.
  The labelled arrow follows Card's reference to its destructor.
  It describes a declaration relation; containment is shown by the folder.
  Non-normative: L2, L4, C2. Synthetic label-card example.
  Other package items and declaration contracts are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
